chives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0018", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.4904, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0022", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.487, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0017", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.4869, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0027", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 0.029, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__business__0038", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "business", "score": 0.9272, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__business__0032", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "business", "score": 0.9056, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__business__0033", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "business", "score": 0.8664, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 88, "dropped_candidates": 784, "token_estimate": 31947, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "All five companies describe regulatory risk around product approval and post-approval developments, plus drug pricing and compliance enforcement. Pfizer cites regulators' interpretation of trial data and approval conditions [PFE_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0020] and pricing measures such as the IRA and EU reform [PFE_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0016]. J&J cites regulatory scrutiny, cGMP issues, and IRA government-established pricing beginning in 2026 [JNJ_10K_2025-12-28__risk_factors__0007][JNJ_10K_2025-12-28__risk_factors__0004]. Merck cites possible FDA/HHS policy changes and the need to obtain and maintain approvals [MRK_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0028], and Lilly cites enforcement changes and cGMP scrutiny [LLY_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0037]. AbbVie cites healthcare policy changes and ongoing compliance with manufacturing, labeling and post-marketing requirements [ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0022]. On how they respond, the context shows Merck's policy advocacy [MRK_10K_2024-12-31__business__0022], Lilly's quality-system investments [LLY_10K_2025-12-31__business__0074] and AbbVie's compliance effort [ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0022]; it states little response for Pfizer or J&J.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "PFE", "company": "Pfizer Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Regulatory interpretation of data, accelerated approval conditions, and post-approval concerns could adversely affect a product's commercial potential (FY2024 10-K, period ended December 31, 2024).", "citations": ["PFE_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0020"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Drug pricing measures (IRA, state PDABs, China VBP, EU pharmaceutical legislation reform) could adversely affect the business.", "citations": ["PFE_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0016"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Pfizer faces government inquiries and enforcement risk; a 2018 Corporate Integrity Agreement expired in May 2023 and the OIG closed the matter in January 2025.", "citations": ["PFE_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0024"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "JNJ", "company": "Johnson & Johnson", "findings": [{"point": "Significant regulatory scrutiny imposes compliance costs; cGMP issues can lead to fines, recalls, shortages and delayed approvals (FY2025 10-K, period ended December 28, 2025).", "citations": ["JNJ_10K_2025-12-28__risk_factors__0007"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The IRA subjects certain products to government-established pricing beginning in 2026, and failure to adhere to the government's interpretations may expose the Company to penalties.", "citations": ["JNJ_10K_2025-12-28__risk_factors__0004"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Regulation is described as trending toward increasingly stringent enforcement, including privacy and cybersecurity laws in the EU and China.", "citations": ["JNJ_10K_2025-12-28__business__0010"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "MRK", "company": "Merck & Co Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Potential U.S. policy and personnel changes at HHS/FDA could make approvals and vaccine recommendations harder (FY2024 10-K, period ended December 31, 2024).", "citations": ["MRK_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0028"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Merck lists exposure to health care reform, FCPA, pricing laws, data privacy and sustainability regulations such as the EU CSRD.", "citations": ["MRK_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0031"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Merck engages in public policy advocacy with policymakers on cost containment.", "citations": ["MRK_10K_2024-12-31__business__0022"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "LLY", "company": "Eli Lilly and Company", "findings": [{"point": "Evolving U.S. and foreign regulatory priorities may increase investigations, litigation and claims, and cGMP issues can lead to recalls, fines and approval delays (FY2025 10-K, period ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["LLY_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0037"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Lilly makes substantial investments in company-wide quality systems and controls to maintain cGMP compliance.", "citations": ["LLY_10K_2025-12-31__business__0074"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Lilly notes U.S. pricing arrangements and policy efforts to align pricing with international benchmarks are uncertain and could reduce revenue in certain markets.", "citations": ["LLY_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0007"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "ABBV", "company": "AbbVie Inc", "findings": [{"point": "AbbVie cannot guarantee ongoing compliance with manufacturing, labeling, advertising and post-marketing requirements, and incurs expense to ensure compliance (FY2024 10-K, period ended December 31, 2024).", "citations": ["ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0022"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Compliance with health care regulations is costly, and failure can lead to delayed launches, recalls and sanctions.", "citations": ["ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__business__0038"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "New safety or efficacy information may require label changes or narrowed indications.", "citations": ["ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0018"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"columns": ["Company", "Key regulatory risk theme", "Stated response in context"], "rows": [["PFE", "Approval interpretation, IRA/EU pricing [PFE_10K_2024-12-31